# .disclose-allow — exemptions for THIS repository's own fixtures, read by the shared disclose
# workflow from the pull request's BASE (so a pull request cannot widen the exemptions that judge
# it). One per line: <rule-glob> <location-glob> <reason of three words or more>. A location glob
# covers a tree path and the same path inside a built tarball. See `devkit disclose --help`.
#
# The gate's own suite plants a value for every generic rule to prove it fires. The private
# addresses are assembled at run time; the MAC, the op:// reference and the address outside the
# RFC 2606 names are written out, synthetic, and the file is the fixture.
email   tests/suites/test_disclose.py  synthetic owner address in the gate's own fixtures
mac     tests/suites/test_disclose.py  synthetic device MAC in the gate's own fixtures
op-ref  tests/suites/test_disclose.py  synthetic op:// reference in the gate's own fixtures
